        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Saint Petersburg</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">1703 CE – present</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Founded</span><span class="info-stat-val">On 27 May 1703 (16 May in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/julian-calendar">Julian calendar</a>) by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tsar">Tsar</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peter-the-great">Peter the Great</a>, who laid down the Peter and Paul Fortress on Zayachy (Hare) Island after capturing the Swedish fortress of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nyenskans">Nyenskans</a>.</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Where</span><span class="info-stat-val">On the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/neva-river">Neva River</a> at the head of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gulf-of-finland">Gulf of Finland</a> on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baltic-sea">Baltic Sea</a>, on the islands of the river's delta and the lowlands along Neva Bay, in north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>.</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Known for</span><span class="info-stat-val"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peter-the-great">Peter the Great</a>'s founding on a captured Swedish site; capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russian-empire">Russian Empire</a>; the Winter Palace and the Hermitage; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/decembrists">Decembrist revolt</a> of 1825; the revolutions of 1905 and 1917; the siege of Leningrad of 1941 to 1944; its canals and bridges</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Today</span><span class="info-stat-val">Saint Petersburg is the second-largest city in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>, after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a>, and is governed as a federal city.</span></div>
